        "### Complexity Analysis of DFS for 8-Puzzle\n",
        "\n",
        "For the 8-puzzle problem, the average branching factor (`b`) can be approximated. In a 3x3 grid, the blank tile has:\n",
        "- 2 possible moves when in a corner (4 corners)\n",
        "- 3 possible moves when on an edge (4 edges)\n",
        "- 4 possible moves when in the center (1 center)\n",
        "\n",
        "Thus, the average branching factor `b` is approximately `(4*2 + 4*3 + 1*4) / 9 = 2.66`.\n",
        "\n",
        "The depth of the solution (`d`) is the number of moves in the path found. The time and space complexity of DFS in the worst case can be exponential, roughly proportional to `b^d`."
      ]
    },
